  ],
  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.1222916666666665,
      "text": "Imagine sharing eleven quarter-sized pieces among a group.",
      "source_sha256": "ae3e849e9c1c121caf8c0985d206eab8f2cc6045035f254fa9b59e4338edcdc4"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.242291666666667,
      "end": 8.226625,
      "text": "Counting pieces is easy, but how many whole units could you build?",
      "source_sha256": "06cb12282e3b7dc689d5ab69b524cc6d81a5e17444dfccd3952cc65ae84b1545"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.346625,
      "end": 11.234625,
      "text": "There's more than one way to name this amount!",
      "source_sha256": "1a752ae227854c8358b30ee617cf2eb627be6b8e025a8e2ccd4c4428d0e11eb2"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.966666666666667,
      "end": 19.420458333333332,
      "text": "Today, we're learning to represent and convert mixed numbers and improper fractions, without changing the amount they describe.",
      "source_sha256": "449cad4910051cd612a3ea4c54e490b310a02e6a76e5a17d99f0fe27e4a74ee7"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.033333333333335,
      "end": 24.378583333333335,
      "text": "You'll group equal pieces to see complete wholes and any extra part.",
      "source_sha256": "e4845a57a7f912b5bb7370a5e61091307305426bca807d5168a9f33d9491cce1"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.6,
      "end": 29.169708333333332,
      "text": "You'll turn an improper fraction into a mixed number, and go back the other way.",
      "source_sha256": "86b7ccc98000a4f5adaf0c2eabd47b426b14545453c53ff8b0f79f685a607ea4"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.4,
      "end": 34.048833333333334,
      "text": "You'll check that both names match the same model or number-line position.",
      "source_sha256": "f1033f61ba9a17aae7b22ed67f74e27a8a3a67f4f3ce46d1c5e9412ea178ca02"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.266666666666666,
      "end": 35.827625,
      "text": "First, choose one whole.",
      "source_sha256": "600fc3595fba8f532d99aa4308fd3124dbc5e478f611185615bea643967b7600"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.947625,
      "end": 38.66575,
      "text": "Its parts must be equal in size.",
      "source_sha256": "41ad9f3d14d84beb28a588e206e9e9fbc749b34a5332ee78931f1fa68b6e0279"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.78575,
      "end": 43.422916666666666,
      "text": "The outline of the model shows the entire whole, not just the coloured share.",
      "source_sha256": "34cb8caf1c2abee5d1f389a76d951c175a9c1f431f9f704f1bb91959617d1298"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.93333333333333,
      "end": 47.14704166666667,
      "text": "Here, three equal parts are chosen out of four.",
      "source_sha256": "1a5948ca564d2a058ed2d8e482a130dea68f1758ac3f4eaef67ecf790f3b0b4c"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.267041666666664,
      "end": 50.861958333333334,
      "text": "The top number, the numerator, counts chosen parts.",
      "source_sha256": "d7559c9cc8969222999bf56e3c7669fcda96560e79c4744375ee260c4b4a0bab"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.98195833333333,
      "end": 55.60125,
      "text": "The bottom number, the denominator, tells how many equal parts make the whole.",
      "source_sha256": "0bf13aa696ee40192b53f341dfa824885ccebaa166f8dd45f0ee925c1b394601"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.233333333333334,
      "end": 59.859833333333334,
      "text": "How many complete wholes can you build from eleven quarters?",
      "source_sha256": "5b2490f5068174bc53713145e98cedb240ee10d15419177d2eb3a0dece5def82"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.97983333333333,
      "end": 63.93454166666667,
      "text": "Group four pieces at a time, and notice any pieces left over.",
      "source_sha256": "c5d2723b1250291643090eaaa8ac6a5cb97885428d1eecdbb8500d98f75e7afc"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.96666666666667,
      "end": 68.97816666666667,
      "text": "Four quarters make one whole.",
      "source_sha256": "8cc385220948d803033da3afaa0508c7b7a99ff2454da4879a3cb18684d03a39"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.09816666666667,
      "end": 71.846,
      "text": "Another four quarters make a second whole.",
      "source_sha256": "7c2fadb0741023a0b7809e850f5466c4939a4093bc6c893210f815be52cd9c9f"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.966,
      "end": 74.07983333333334,
      "text": "Three quarters are left over.",
      "source_sha256": "dc296fe3a3222977869133d01d265fcb7b44df6b9de14222becd58bcd00a05b5"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.43333333333334,
      "end": 77.55783333333333,
      "text": "Eleven quarters is an improper fraction.",
      "source_sha256": "80935518661452ac7d49b10dddb19db82662a900939c218db783f4d4e2fad071"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.67783333333334,
      "end": 81.48583333333333,
      "text": "Its numerator is at least as large as its denominator.",
      "source_sha256": "dffc44e360e8aa4e593e858c0b1bf805bf0a7e88e9bcc2e92d5f7dcdae70b719"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.60583333333334,
      "end": 84.16804166666667,
      "text": "It can describe one whole or more.",
      "source_sha256": "94a3640971e31c75cc31537ed79a5757f8dc896a7084703e660ed49f33979e2e"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.53333333333333,
      "end": 87.31166666666667,
      "text": "Two and three quarters is a mixed number.",
      "source_sha256": "cb9273370cddde14cf9f84ba03702075e70c732dee17af514ae50bdedd348bc6"
    },
    {
      "start": 87.43166666666667,
      "end": 90.8305,
      "text": "It combines two whole units with a fractional part.",
      "source_sha256": "8e9a1f9a6ad6d12de0aa05d4664a7a4d1c790606c51ef534115e1d610b26e3f3"
    },
    {
      "start": 91.2,
      "end": 93.9445,
      "text": "To convert, divide eleven by four.",
      "source_sha256": "72540964cfa158dc7500ca409f8ee09ca7aac651f2c07c2e54e2547ed652d5ab"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.0645,
      "end": 97.99566666666666,
      "text": "Eleven divided by four is two with a remainder of three.",
      "source_sha256": "1e0b11848482b98781f53267ba74ae5f5405ef19551fd164dc53331ed0eb6ead"
    },
    {
      "start": 98.36666666666666,
      "end": 102.43091666666666,
      "text": "The denominator stays four because our pieces are still quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "0f10c1f246f0a2774c34c5042f64172a884304d64334ff6da5aea6f78c5c8d79"
    },
    {
      "start": 102.55091666666667,
      "end": 105.89154166666667,
      "text": "So eleven quarters equals two and three quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "a16668537250d0f6e93185f94d55f6deb6b20352a7a570bf6b0af2d777e8e5f7"
    },
    {
      "start": 106.26666666666667,
      "end": 109.78683333333333,
      "text": "The remainder counts extra quarter-sized pieces.",
      "source_sha256": "da14eaeabbd0b76c85737073cd4bb26c536cb5c1331819fa0d86479649a483bf"
    },
    {
      "start": 109.90683333333334,
      "end": 112.34595833333333,
      "text": "It doesn't become the denominator.",
      "source_sha256": "6d5eb61262ca000cb0f6a88f8f201014c2edd3dcb7bb65b6f89a77305d05cabe"
    },
    {
      "start": 112.46595833333333,
      "end": 117.085625,
      "text": "A picture helps you see two complete wholes and three quarters of the next one.",
      "source_sha256": "de29dd33f3098f96d8f3aeac70798f90209c98f5f954d93725e9d6d1d25357f2"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.76666666666667,
      "end": 122.288375,
      "text": "How could you count all the fifth-sized pieces in three and two fifths?",
      "source_sha256": "50ad57f53377d6595f58ae4c16f9410a494a51dcf3efbe94078d2cdcd690b8c2"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.408375,
      "end": 125.59191666666666,
      "text": "Remember that each whole contains five fifths.",
      "source_sha256": "cecd6fbc2bfba176b12de8e15aa9fd11d38854d11cd26a424eaa8d185377cd3f"
    },
    {
      "start": 128.6,
      "end": 130.38216666666668,
      "text": "Now go the other way.",
      "source_sha256": "4052810dae34648c2b307bb34e86dc6c2de4a4a286c88619973074055cabf197"
    },
    {
      "start": 130.50216666666665,
      "end": 132.54333333333332,
      "text": "Take three and two fifths.",
      "source_sha256": "623959d3d7a48d3310f16446bb01e8f8e73b86e4b4baf63885e7f71f773fe420"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.66333333333333,
      "end": 134.99454166666666,
      "text": "Each whole contains five fifths.",
      "source_sha256": "97076932318675ff17e9e91f3e03257d55aa0e3526172545933954fbb806082d"
    },
    {
      "start": 135.36666666666667,
      "end": 138.087,
      "text": "Three times five gives fifteen fifths.",
      "source_sha256": "581b8b183faea693da68edf44063c8f295aca1b56bec182cd1f18f8968c25588"
    },
    {
      "start": 138.207,
      "end": 141.72404166666666,
      "text": "Add the extra two fifths to make seventeen fifths.",
      "source_sha256": "622d7724dbb2d256c3ce08df34d69f1f0015398d6b5a0f052ca0adfc73d8aa17"
    },
    {
      "start": 142.1,
      "end": 145.731875,
      "text": "So three and two fifths equals seventeen fifths.",
      "source_sha256": "9044f1eeec7afb2850510f55f822958ea5bdfe743b9bee0c7a0775d619ba9c16"
    },
    {
      "start": 145.851875,
      "end": 151.255625,
      "text": "Multiply the whole number by the denominator, add the numerator, and keep the denominator.",
      "source_sha256": "65fbc05a8ea1bdac2126e2eb75b74cb1d94ce59b929716d7c3f065373b2b8dfb"
    },
    {
      "start": 151.63333333333333,
      "end": 155.494125,
      "text": "Counting in fifths doesn't change the whole or the amount.",
      "source_sha256": "f081f74b8fad2053edce5d3bfa25dfa113ba53d60ae88d1004846b321d35618c"
    },
    {
      "start": 155.614125,
      "end": 160.77975,
      "text": "It simply replaces the whole-number groups with a single count of equal pieces.",
      "source_sha256": "8e941307eb85d7a96457e377bfe3a6f81341da98b0df363929c4c81244a46ff2"
    },
    {
      "start": 161.43333333333334,
      "end": 166.013,
      "text": "A mixed number isn't made by adding its whole number to its numerator.",
      "source_sha256": "94e67ad60e166aacc47912a79d21e197a64b2a03f13beda85faedb5275a95dd0"
    },
    {
      "start": 166.133,
      "end": 169.34379166666668,
      "text": "Two and three quarters is not five quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "983374bbaaf0bf64c7baa8eba3ea8b9532147b6d722738f3b8d40612d89e2b95"
    },
    {
      "start": 169.46379166666668,
      "end": 172.6955,
      "text": "The two wholes already contain eight quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "08aa5cb18ccb9d4623a08e5564c33f911a9168905ade0c347c2ba3044ccdd98e"
    },
    {
      "start": 173.36666666666667,
      "end": 176.78858333333332,
      "text": "Eight quarters plus three quarters is eleven quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "3abb29fc24f88634b08124dbdbc3b1dbb0ccca30807ed2ae1edac912d4857642"
    },
    {
      "start": 176.90858333333333,
      "end": 182.59066666666666,
      "text": "That's why we multiply the whole number by the denominator, then add the extra numerator.",
      "source_sha256": "e5ac5e4c2ebdd6258ca8d3c7c6f8851d6041ce0ca4d78e0f5dca6545d51392da"
    },
    {
      "start": 183.26666666666668,
      "end": 186.540875,
      "text": "A fraction can also equal an exact whole.",
      "source_sha256": "3d1da62a670f4d3ece3f97a1215eb95e6a091f0775cdf441e1eeaa0038e1a11e"
    },
    {
      "start": 186.660875,
      "end": 190.78079166666666,
      "text": "Eight quarters is two wholes, with no fractional part left over.",
      "source_sha256": "762d29f18de15b5b1feac1a52b7e79b03e52a993cdd146bcba775cc06c42ba1b"
    },
    {
      "start": 191.13333333333333,
      "end": 194.54983333333334,
      "text": "To compare mixed numbers, compare the wholes first.",
      "source_sha256": "0de53731d7ba6b5884e4dad933c672d69254c8e549f59309494180b04c40136f"
    },
    {
      "start": 194.66983333333334,
      "end": 198.36875,
      "text": "Three and one quarter is greater than two and three quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "381d278d8d8881d32e6b664fec38feca9e3687f63fa3d729702bb1c2ee2ba34c"
    },
    {
      "start": 198.73333333333332,
      "end": 201.97566666666665,
      "text": "If the wholes match, compare the fractional parts.",
      "source_sha256": "2ea76c0f6034abf60a69b26441046b33885a651a46c171b911c8e4fbb7650985"
    },
    {
      "start": 202.09566666666666,
      "end": 205.4565,
      "text": "Two and one half is greater than two and one quarter.",
      "source_sha256": "f648059cf9cb0116b22b9c891948a61fd9eb3d8bedd44dd20a620d7fee31ef46"
    },
    {
      "start": 205.83333333333334,
      "end": 209.16933333333333,
      "text": "A number line helps us check amounts beyond one.",
      "source_sha256": "97513664eb8ad692ed412aea1c30168b22c6039eb6c7a32bc96e74b9b65202c9"
    },
    {
      "start": 209.28933333333333,
      "end": 212.83270833333333,
      "text": "Two and one half is ten quarter-steps from zero.",
      "source_sha256": "added08b204a9354daf31283c1982754ea8bc4c3cc8a45119f1847b20c1a2a2b"
    },
    {
      "start": 212.95270833333333,
      "end": 216.76108333333335,
      "text": "Two and three quarters is one quarter-step further to the right.",
      "source_sha256": "5eb3b373455fd829478aa6f0cfbbbda0fdb78a1647bbaf74c624a581939c6bce"
    },
    {
      "start": 217.43333333333334,
      "end": 220.72058333333334,
      "text": "How many wholes and quarters are in nine quarters?",
      "source_sha256": "f78435202a8a3ae864ca51286b214290bfadf795f2243ace5a67d8849eeb3595"
    },
    {
      "start": 225.73333333333332,
      "end": 228.707875,
      "text": "Nine quarters is two wholes and one quarter.",
      "source_sha256": "fc53e950ac6f4a822a9b60e3352c320e561ddc3a6f5ba4bf1d1c1c3ef5d411c9"
    },
    {
      "start": 229.06666666666666,
      "end": 233.0205,
      "text": "Our goal was to connect mixed numbers and improper fractions.",
      "source_sha256": "48757ed1692f667d69703e20f9159a4240d0df75d6192e66297546b075d26382"
    },
    {
      "start": 233.1405,
      "end": 237.93016666666668,
      "text": "You can build wholes, count the leftover parts, and convert in either direction.",
      "source_sha256": "e39e245d88c022bf31474904a0b98eafeda8fe42fe92e450fbf40e21ff74d032"
    },
    {
      "start": 238.05016666666666,
      "end": 241.23720833333334,
      "text": "Before calculating, what would your amount look like?",
      "source_sha256": "9d1ea76b72ec7f3b1f7b0d2d730e2b588aa172b76654e4bc5b28179f5dccb4ed"
    },
    {
      "start": 241.35720833333335,
      "end": 244.63779166666666,
      "text": "Try drawing it, then practise on Math Magic.",
      "source_sha256": "7eafda4caaa1586b32fe4c14fc8055a79a51c642d8f028e11a53eab7cc7c8c22"
    }
  ],
